@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il08-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il08-tax-years`
IMPORT `ito-s64b-s65-registered-spouse`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests for ss 64B and 65. Row IL-08. Expected values from lines 2440-2448; none edited to match
-- the code.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — sections 64B and 65`

§§ `Section 64B`

GIVEN `first` IS A NUMBER
      `second` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A couple, for section 64B`
`a couple whose incomes two years before were` `first` `and` `second` MEANS
    `A couple, for section 64B` WITH
        `the first tax year in question`                        IS 2026
        `the first spouse's taxable income two tax years before it`  IS `first`
        `the second spouse's taxable income two tax years before it` IS `second`

-- (a): 120,000 of 180,000 is more than half; 60,000 is not.
#ASSERT `s 64B(a) — the assessing officer may determine that` `the first spouse` `is the registered spouse of` (`a couple whose incomes two years before were` 120000 `and` 60000)
#ASSERT NOT `s 64B(a) — the assessing officer may determine that` `the second spouse` `is the registered spouse of` (`a couple whose incomes two years before were` 120000 `and` 60000)
-- Equal incomes: neither is more than half (fork F32), and (c) needs both at nil.
#ASSERT NOT `s 64B(a) — the assessing officer may determine that` `the first spouse` `is the registered spouse of` (`a couple whose incomes two years before were` 50000 `and` 50000)
#ASSERT NOT `s 64B(c) — neither spouse had taxable income two tax years before, so the assessing officer may determine either, for` (`a couple whose incomes two years before were` 50000 `and` 50000)
-- (c): neither had income.
#ASSERT `s 64B(c) — neither spouse had taxable income two tax years before, so the assessing officer may determine either, for` (`a couple whose incomes two years before were` 0 `and` 0)

GIVEN `joint`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day`    IS A DATE
      `elected`    IS A NUMBER
      `other`      IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An election of the registered spouse, for section 64B(b)`
`an election for 2027, joint and in writing:` `joint` `, notice on` `the day` `, the elected spouse having earned` `elected` `against` `other` MEANS
    `An election of the registered spouse, for section 64B(b)` WITH
        `the spouse elected to be registered`                           IS `the second spouse`
        `made jointly and in writing by both spouses`                   IS `joint`
        `the day the notice was given`                                  IS `the day`
        `the first tax year it is to govern`                            IS 2027
        `that spouse's income in the tax year before the notice year`   IS `elected`
        `the other spouse's income in the tax year before the notice year` IS `other`

-- (b): notice by 1 October 2026 for 2027, and the elected spouse's 2025 income at least 25% of the other's.
#ASSERT `s 64B(b) — the election is one the couple may make:` (`an election for 2027, joint and in writing:` TRUE `, notice on` (YMD 2026 10 1) `, the elected spouse having earned` 25000 `against` 100000)
#ASSERT NOT `s 64B(b) — the election is one the couple may make:` (`an election for 2027, joint and in writing:` TRUE `, notice on` (YMD 2026 10 2) `, the elected spouse having earned` 25000 `against` 100000)
#ASSERT NOT `s 64B(b) — the election is one the couple may make:` (`an election for 2027, joint and in writing:` TRUE `, notice on` (YMD 2026 10 1) `, the elected spouse having earned` 24999 `against` 100000)
#ASSERT NOT `s 64B(b) — the election is one the couple may make:` (`an election for 2027, joint and in writing:` FALSE `, notice on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `, the elected spouse having earned` 50000 `against` 100000)

-- (d)(1): at least five tax years, 2024 to 2028.
#ASSERT `s 64B(d)(1) — a determination or election first governing tax year` 2024 `still stands, unless they cease to be spouses or the Director decides, in tax year` 2028
#ASSERT NOT `s 64B(d)(1) — a determination or election first governing tax year` 2024 `still stands, unless they cease to be spouses or the Director decides, in tax year` 2029
-- (d)(2): the elected spouse's income under 25% of the other's in a year.
#ASSERT `s 64B(d)(2) — the assessing officer may determine the registered spouse for the year, the elected spouse having income` 20000 `against` 100000
#ASSERT NOT `s 64B(d)(2) — the assessing officer may determine the registered spouse for the year, the elected spouse having income` 25000 `against` 100000

§§ `Section 65`

`his salary, 180,000`                  MEANS `An item of a household's income, for section 65` WITH `whose` IS `the registered spouse's`, `kind` IS `any other income`, `taxable amount` IS 180000, `from assets received by inheritance, or originating in compensation or insurance money received for bodily injury` IS FALSE
`her salary, 50,000`                   MEANS `An item of a household's income, for section 65` WITH `whose` IS `the other spouse's`, `kind` IS `any other income`, `taxable amount` IS 50000, `from assets received by inheritance, or originating in compensation or insurance money received for bodily injury` IS FALSE
`a child of 10's interest, 1,000`      MEANS `An item of a household's income, for section 65` WITH `whose` IS `a child's, of the registered spouse` 10, `kind` IS `interest, discount or linkage differences`, `taxable amount` IS 1000, `from assets received by inheritance, or originating in compensation or insurance money received for bodily injury` IS FALSE
`a child of 10's interest on an inheritance, 1,000` MEANS `An item of a household's income, for section 65` WITH `whose` IS `a child's, of the registered spouse` 10, `kind` IS `interest, discount or linkage differences`, `taxable amount` IS 1000, `from assets received by inheritance, or originating in compensation or insurance money received for bodily injury` IS TRUE
`a child of 10's transparent-company income from an inheritance, 500` MEANS `An item of a household's income, for section 65` WITH `whose` IS `a child's, of the registered spouse` 10, `kind` IS `income from a transparent company as defined in section 64A1`, `taxable amount` IS 500, `from assets received by inheritance, or originating in compensation or insurance money received for bodily injury` IS TRUE
`a child of 18's capital gain, 2,000`  MEANS `An item of a household's income, for section 65` WITH `whose` IS `a child's, of the registered spouse` 18, `kind` IS `capital gain`, `taxable amount` IS 2000, `from assets received by inheritance, or originating in compensation or insurance money received for bodily injury` IS FALSE
`a child of 10's wages, 3,000`         MEANS `An item of a household's income, for section 65` WITH `whose` IS `a child's, of the registered spouse` 10, `kind` IS `any other income`, `taxable amount` IS 3000, `from assets received by inheritance, or originating in compensation or insurance money received for bodily injury` IS FALSE

-- Row IL-07's H11: the registered father's 180,000 salary, a housewife with no income: 180,000.
#ASSERT `s 65 — the income charged in the registered spouse's name, in tax year` 2026 `, from` (LIST `his salary, 180,000`) EQUALS 180000
-- Both spouses' income is the registered spouse's: 230,000.
#ASSERT `s 65 — the income charged in the registered spouse's name, in tax year` 2026 `, from` (LIST `his salary, 180,000`, `her salary, 50,000`) EQUALS 230000
-- A child of 10's interest counts; on an inheritance it does not; transparent-company income counts
-- even from an inheritance (the exception does not name it, fork F33); a child of 18's capital gain
-- does not; a child's wages are not one of the four kinds.
#ASSERT `s 65 — the income charged in the registered spouse's name, in tax year` 2026 `, from` (LIST `his salary, 180,000`, `a child of 10's interest, 1,000`) EQUALS 181000
#ASSERT `s 65 — the income charged in the registered spouse's name, in tax year` 2026 `, from` (LIST `his salary, 180,000`, `a child of 10's interest on an inheritance, 1,000`) EQUALS 180000
#ASSERT `s 65 — the income charged in the registered spouse's name, in tax year` 2026 `, from` (LIST `his salary, 180,000`, `a child of 10's transparent-company income from an inheritance, 500`) EQUALS 180500
#ASSERT `s 65 — the income charged in the registered spouse's name, in tax year` 2026 `, from` (LIST `his salary, 180,000`, `a child of 18's capital gain, 2,000`) EQUALS 180000
#ASSERT `s 65 — the income charged in the registered spouse's name, in tax year` 2026 `, from` (LIST `his salary, 180,000`, `a child of 10's wages, 3,000`) EQUALS 180000
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 65 — the income charged in the registered spouse's name, in tax year` 2023 `, from` (LIST `his salary, 180,000`) BECAUSE "row IL-08 does not hold the text of these sections for a tax year before 2024"
